      "id": "sol.ahsme-1954-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Setting \\(a=b=1\\) makes every monomial equal to \\(1,\\) so the value of the expansion equals the sum of its coefficients. Thus the sum is \\[ (1+1)^6=64. \\]\n\nThe correct answer is C.",
